# Released ptah binaries read the advisory snapshots below live from master
# (internal/advisorysource.DefaultLocation), so a change merged here reaches
# every installed binary without a release. The rules below notify the
# repository owner of each change to the snapshots, to the code that fetches
# and validates them, to the workflow that proposes a refresh, and to this
# file. They are a notification, not a protection: GitHub enforces nothing
# here unless branch protection requires code-owner review, and an author
# cannot approve their own pull request. What protects a scan is the rule the
# binary applies, vulnerability.EvaluateVersionedWithFloor: each advisory is
# matched against a copy read from master and against the snapshot built into
# the binary, and the stricter answer is reported, so a copy can add a finding
# but cannot make a result cleaner than the built-in snapshot.

/internal/vulnerability/*.json @denisvmedia
/internal/advisorysource/ @denisvmedia
/.github/workflows/security-snapshots.yml @denisvmedia
/.github/CODEOWNERS @denisvmedia
